      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Amos Bartlett, the first postmaster, gave the community his name, honoring his early role in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartlett%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits at the crossroads of State Routes 550 and 555, just south of Coal Run, a tributary of Wolf Creek.",
